{"explanation":"Add a focused EncryptedKey API round-trip regression test while preserving the existing test() and testUTF8() method signatures and assertions unchanged. Successful decryption through the unchanged interface demonstrates that the encryption-time GCM parameters were retained in a form decrypt can consume; the encoding and algorithm assertions verify the existing AAD-protected key reconstruction contract.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey exposes no public accessor for retained Cipher AlgorithmParameters; therefore, successful decrypt(key) is the available non-reflective observation that retained explicit-GCM parameters remain available to decryption.","Supported Android providers accept the coordinated EncryptedKey explicit GCMParameterSpec setup and retain AlgorithmParameters in a representation decrypt can decode.","Persisted file-format compatibility is preserved by the coordinated production change retaining the existing EncryptedKey parameter and AAD representation."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","original_code":"    @Test
