","edit_kind":"test","corrected_code":"    @Test
    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes();

        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");
        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);

        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);
        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();
        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);
    }

    @Test
    public void testExplicitGcmParameterRoundTrip() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey plaintext = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey encryptionKey = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey encryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintext);
        SecretKey decryptedKey = encryptedKey.decrypt(encryptionKey);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(plaintext.getEncoded(), decryptedKey.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(plaintext.getAlgorithm(), decryptedKey.getAlgorithm());
    }
","reason":"Exercise the unchanged EncryptedKey.encrypt/decrypt interface after explicit GCM parameter initialization. The successful round trip requires encryption-time parameters to remain available to decrypt, while the retained encoding and algorithm assertions verify the existing AAD-protected key restoration behavior without asserting fresh ciphertext, nonce, or parameter bytes.","symbol":"EncryptedKeyTest.testExplicitGcmParameterRoundTrip"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["EncryptedKeyTest preserves the existing test() and testUTF8() public test method signatures and all existing assertions.","EncryptedKeyTest adds non-reflective coverage that the unchanged EncryptedKey interface round-trips a protected HmacSHA512 key through AES/GCM encryption and decryption.","The added regression test asserts restored key encoding and algorithm without assuming deterministic ciphertext, nonce, or serialized GCM parameters."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey.encrypt must retain its public name, parameter order, return type, and declared checked-exception contract.","EncryptedKey.encrypt must initialize AES/GCM with a fresh explicit GCMParameterSpec and retain parameters compatible with decrypt.","EncryptedKey.decrypt must continue consuming retained parameters and authenticating the protected key algorithm as AAD.","MasterKey must continue supplying an AES KeyGenerator-origin key to EncryptedKey.encrypt while preserving its public entry points and persisted representation."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","required_tests":["Run EncryptedKeyTest.test(), EncryptedKeyTest.testUTF8(), and EncryptedKeyTest.testExplicitGcmParameterRoundTrip() as Android instrumentation tests.","Run the coordinated MasterKeyTest and KeyStoreAccessTest instrumentation regressions on supported Android providers.","Compile mobile androidTest sources and run the patched module Gradle test tasks."]}
